{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>For</b> — Rabbi Moses said: [the reading is] רגעי ארץ בקיעי ארץ, and the sense is an allusion to what is hidden, and like it: עורי רגע וימאס (Psalm 73:20, \"Awake, O Lord, and despise\")."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :register {:flags {0 ["Lord"]}}, :notes {0 "The citation from Psalm 73:20 is reversed in word order; Ibn Ezra's point appears to be that רגע there likewise carries a cryptic sense related to 'stillness/silence.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:41.215106072Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}